# mbsync (isync 1.5.1) configuration - fetches mail from Gmail's IMAP into
# the maildir in the shared maildir-data volume, authenticating with an
# OAuth2 (XOAUTH2) token fetched from the pizauth daemon.
#
# The pizauth account name in PassCmd must match the account block in
# pizauth/pizauth.conf.  The maildir is indexed by the notmuch container,
# so mail sent via msmtp shows up in the index once mbsync fetches the
# [Gmail]/Sent Mail folder.
#
# Syntax notes (isync 1.5.1, not modern isync):
#   - sections are delimited by blank lines
#   - the IMAP account is an "IMAPStore" (not "IMAPAccount")
#   - the maildir root is "Path" (not "Maildir"); with SubFolders Verbatim
#     it must have a trailing slash (mailbox "Sent" lands at Path/Sent);
#     "Inbox" is not relative to Path, so it is set explicitly
#   - mailbox pairs are "Channel"s with "Far :store:box" / "Near :store:box"
#     (a leading colon is mandatory; box names with spaces are quoted)
#   - "TLSType IMAPS" = implicit TLS on port 993
#   - the xoauth2 SASL plugin (see Containerfile) registers the XOAUTH2
#     mechanism with cyrus-sasl; it builds the RFC 6278 response from the
#     raw token that PassCmd outputs

# Everything is pulled; only FLAG changes are ever pushed.
#
# "Sync" otherwise defaults to Full ("New Upgrade Gone Flags") in both
# directions, and the push half is pure liability here:
#   - PushNew re-uploaded 1,229 old messages to Gmail on 2026-09-15 after the
#     sync state was lost, and would upload all 409k of /var/mail/Archive if a
#     channel were ever added for Gmail's own "Archive" label (Path +
#     SubFolders Verbatim resolve ":gmail-local:Archive" to that directory).
#   - PushGone means deleting maildir files marks the far-side copies \Deleted,
#     which is why deduplicating the maildir required fast-forwarding the state
#     first.
# Neither is wanted: msmtp sends the mail, Gmail files it under
# [Gmail]/Sent Mail, and the sent channel pulls it back.
#
# PushFlags is kept deliberately: notmuch runs with synchronize_flags = true,
# so reading or starring mail locally rewrites maildir flags, and those should
# still reach Gmail.  Flag changes cannot duplicate or delete mail.
# (Compound direction+type flags per mbsync(1): each asserts one cell.)
Sync PullNew PullUpgrade PullGone PullFlags PushFlags
Create Both
Expunge None

IMAPStore gmail
Host imap.gmail.com
User aeroevan@gmail.com
PassCmd "pizauth show aeroevan@gmail.com"
AuthMechs XOAUTH2
TLSType IMAPS
PipelineDepth 1
# The default is 20s, which produced a steady stream of "Socket error on
# imap.gmail.com: timeout" during the bulk backfill, each one killing the run
# mid-sync.  Gmail throttles hard once the 2500 MB/day cap is in sight, so give
# it room to answer.
Timeout 120

MaildirStore gmail-local
Path /var/mail/
Inbox /var/mail/INBOX
SubFolders Verbatim

Channel inbox
Far :gmail:INBOX
Near :gmail-local:INBOX

Channel sent
Far ":gmail:[Gmail]/Sent Mail"
Near :gmail-local:Sent
